title: "Submit a Site Inspection Report with photos"
config:
  theme: base
  sequence:
    actorMargin: 75
    boxMargin: 12
    diagramMarginX: 45
    diagramMarginY: 30
    messageMargin: 40
    noteMargin: 16
    mirrorActors: false
    width: 190
    height: 90
  themeVariables:
    background: "#ffffff"
    primaryColor: "#69a8ef"
    primaryBorderColor: "#333333"
    primaryTextColor: "#111111"
    actorBkg: "#69a8ef"
    actorBorder: "#333333"
    actorTextColor: "#111111"
    actorLineColor: "#555555"
    signalColor: "#333333"
    signalTextColor: "#111111"
    activationBkgColor: "#cdd3db"
    activationBorderColor: "#cdd3db"
    noteBkgColor: "#ffe344"
    noteBorderColor: "#d4ba24"
    noteTextColor: "#111111"
    labelBoxBkgColor: "#ffffff"
    labelBoxBorderColor: "#555555"
    labelTextColor: "#111111"
    loopTextColor: "#111111"
    altBackground: "#ffffff"
  themeCSS: |
    .actor-line {
      stroke-dasharray: 10 10 !important;
      stroke-width: 1.25px !important;
    }
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Steward
    participant Page as New report page<br/>/detail/[namesite]/new-report
    participant Actions as Server actions<br/>utils/supabase/queries.ts
    participant Presign as POST /api/s3/presign
    participant DB as Supabase DB
    participant S3 as AWS S3

    Note over Steward,S3: Covers the SIR submission (inherited, changed in Sprint 2 by #148 and #242). All steps exist on main as of October 11, 2026.<br/>The server actions use the service role, so each write checks the caller first.

    Steward->>Page: Select Submit
    Page->>Page: Check the required questions and the photo fields<br/>(caption, date, photographer). Stop and show the missing items
    Page->>Actions: getCurrentSiteId(namesite), getDateOfVisitQuestionId()
    Actions->>DB: Active site that is not archived
    Page->>Actions: addSiteInspectionReport(siteId, inspectionDate)
    Actions->>Actions: requireApprovedCaller. The owner is the caller, not a browser value
    Actions->>DB: Site is active and not archived?
    Actions->>DB: rpc get_max_inspection_number(year)
    Actions->>DB: Insert form_responses {site_id, user_id, inspection_no, inspection_date}
    DB-->>Page: responseId

    loop Each photo
        Page->>Presign: {filename, contentType, fileSize, siteId, responseId,<br/>questionId, siteName, date, photographer, identifier}
        Presign->>Presign: Signed in? Type JPEG, PNG or WebP? At most 10 MB?<br/>Key inspections/siteId/responseId/questionId/file?
        Presign-->>Page: uploadUrl (180 s), key, generatedFilename
        Page->>S3: PUT the file with uploadUrl
    end

    Page->>Actions: uploadSiteInspectionAnswers(answers)
    Actions->>Actions: requireReportWriter(responseId): owner or Admin, report not archived
    Actions->>DB: Insert answers
    Page->>Actions: insertInspectionAttachments(rows)
    Actions->>Actions: requireReportWriter. Each key must be in the folder<br/>of its site, report and question
    Actions->>DB: Insert attachments

    alt Every step succeeds
        Page->>Page: Remove the saved draft
        Page-->>Steward: Go to /sites?submitted=true
    else A step fails after the report was made
        Page->>Actions: rollbackSiteInspectionSubmission(responseId)
        Actions->>Actions: requireReportWriter. The report must be less than 30 minutes old
        Actions->>DB: Read the attachment rows of the report
        Actions->>DB: Delete attachments, answers, then form_responses
        Actions->>S3: deleteObjectsByKeys(keys of the attachment rows)
        Page-->>Steward: The page logs the error and enables Submit again.<br/>It shows no error message. The draft stays
    end

    Note over Page,S3: The rollback deletes only the S3 files that have an attachment row.<br/>A photo that reached S3 before insertInspectionAttachments failed stays in S3 with no row.
